The mmesh residue in checksummed migrations
-------------------------------------------

The product was named Muninn Mesh (mmesh) until 2026-08-26. Six applied
database migrations under server/src/munarium-store-pg/migrations/ still mention
mmesh in comments: 0002_ledger, 0006_retrieval, 0010_identity_interactions,
0015_storage_backend_vocab, 0016_interactions_instance and 0019_authoring_drafts.
sqlx validates a checksum per applied migration, so editing one byte of an
applied migration stops the server booting against any existing database; the
name therefore survives in those comments, and only there, by design. For the
same reason a few migration comments, in the server and in Matrix, keep
internal work-item identifiers from before the first release.

